---
// Page shell for /personal-finance/risk-tolerance: intro + the
// RiskToleranceLab island (ability/willingness/need questionnaire).
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import RiskToleranceLab from "../../components/RiskToleranceLab.tsx";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import RegionNote from "../../components/RegionNote.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Risk Tolerance Questionnaire"
  description="Answer six short questions to see where you sit on the risk/return spectrum and a suggested stock/bond starting point — scored across your ability, willingness, and need to take risk."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personal Finance · Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>How much risk actually fits you?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The single biggest investing decision is how much to keep in stocks versus
      bonds — and the right answer isn't just about nerve. It blends what you can
      <em>afford</em> to lose, what you can <em>stomach</em>, and what your goal
      truly <em>needs</em>. Six quick questions place you on the spectrum and
      suggest a starting point.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <RegionNote kind="data">
      The questions and the three-dimension framing are universal, but the
      best/worst-year outcome ranges use US market history (1928–present). Expect
      similar shapes, not identical numbers, in other markets.
    </RegionNote>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <RiskToleranceLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Three dimensions, and the one that binds</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Ability</strong> is your capacity to absorb a loss: a long
          horizon, a stable income, and a healthy cash cushion all let you ride
          out downturns without being forced to sell.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Willingness</strong> is your temperament: whether a 30% drop
          makes you sell in a panic or shrug. The best portfolio is worthless if
          you abandon it at the bottom.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Need</strong> is how much return the goal actually requires.
          Taking more risk than you need to reach the goal adds danger without
          purpose.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When these disagree, the <strong>lower</strong> of ability and willingness
        usually wins — there's no point taking risk you can't afford or can't sit
        through. Treat the suggested allocation as a starting point for thought,
        then explore the trade-off in the
        <a href="/tools/portfolio">Asset Allocation tool</a>. This is educational
        only and not personalized financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="risk-tolerance" />

  <section class="container pf-related">
    <h2 class="pf-related-heading">Keep exploring</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid--2 pf-related-grid">
      <li>
        <a href="/tools/portfolio" class="card">
          <h3>Put the allocation to work</h3>
          <p>Take your stock/bond starting point into the Portfolio tool and see the risk/return trade-off it implies.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/personal-finance/money-basics#net-worth" class="card">
          <h3>Know where you stand today</h3>
          <p>Your ability to take risk starts with the full picture — what you own, what you owe, and the cushion in between.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro { padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md); max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--color-text-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .wl-explainer { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
  .pf-related { margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .pf-related-heading { font-size: var(--step-1); padding-bottom: var(--space-xs); border-bottom: var(--border); margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .pf-related-grid { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .pf-related-grid a.card { height: 100%; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; display: block; }
  .pf-related-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .pf-related-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .rt-controls { gap: var(--space-md); }
  .rt-q {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .rt-q-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .rt-q-num {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1.4rem;
    height: 1.4rem;
    margin-right: 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 700;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .rt-opts {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }
  .rt-opt {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;
    border: var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color var(--transition), background var(--transition), color var(--transition);
  }
  .rt-opt:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
  .rt-opt.active {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* Result spectrum */
  .rt-spectrum {
    position: relative;
    height: 0.85rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--color-link), var(--color-accent), var(--color-warn));
    opacity: 0.9;
  }
  .rt-spectrum-marker {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    width: 1.15rem;
    height: 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-text);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  }
  .rt-spectrum-ends {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .rt-flag {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-warn);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-warn);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-warn) 10%, var(--color-surface));
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .rt-flag strong { color: var(--color-text); }

  .rt-placeholder {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .rt-progress {
    height: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .rt-progress-fill {
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    transition: width var(--transition);
  }
</style>
